A. Commit message:
btrfs: backport swap activation rescheduling to avoid core monopolization

B. Change summary:
This patch backports the addition of a voluntary reschedule during swap file activation to prevent monopolizing a CPU core when processing thousands of extents. The change ensures that the system remains responsive by yielding the CPU periodically.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/fs/btrfs/inode.c b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
index 4675f43..c4675f4 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
@@ -10078,6 +10078,8 @@ static int btrfs_swap_activate(struct swap_info_struct *sis, struct file *file,
 			ret = -EINTR;
 			goto out;
 		}
+
+		cond_resched();
 	}
 
 	if (bsi.block_len)
```